: "Lead placement and artifact"}]}, {"id": "b0b7ee4f-4d3c-4744-9811-ce10f5825b8c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Exercise cardiovascular response", "description": "Learners connect cardiac output and blood flow to activity intensity.", "children": [{"id": "a63336da-1d40-481b-972f-74b3681ec7ba", "type": "concept", "title": "Heart rate, stroke volume, cardiac output"}, {"id": "ea17c123-55ba-49cb-9025-d0388d8c3845", "type": "concept", "title": "Blood redistribution during exercise"}, {"id": "7f770d8a-395d-4838-b921-1947b40522cf", "type": "concept", "title": "Recovery kinetics and training status"}]}]}, {"id": "66530fe6-3213-4e0f-a9c4-1a92e3c740c2", "type": "topic", "title": "Respiratory Anatomy, Ventilation, Gas Exchange, and Acid-Base Balance", "description": "Understand how the respiratory system supports oxygen delivery, carbon dioxide removal, and pH regulation.", "children": [{"id": "653cc4ad-607c-46f5-8e44-6a54b7c745db", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Respiratory anatomy", "description": "Students learn the structures that move air and exchange gases.", "children": [{"id": "f9496c9c-5703-4514-ad36-253ebc16b024", "type": "concept", "title": "Upper and lower airways"}, {"id": "6272130b-7914-4f60-b4fc-5f2045f88583", "type": "concept", "title": "Lungs, pleura, alveoli, and respiratory membrane"}, {"id": "c3e23696-7284-4d7a-8849-cd60b13e0e53", "type": "concept", "title": "Respiratory muscles and thoracic mechanics"}]}, {"id": "fa644b56-92fc-44e6-967d-66328404c65e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Ventilation and gas exchange", "description": "This subtopic explains how air movement becomes oxygen delivery.", "children": [{"id": "304951a9-f082-4032-a806-38b736d6ef75", "type": "concept", "title": "Inspiration, expiration, compliance, resistance, and surfactant"}, {"id": "9374600b-7e8a-4eea-b30a-7acdc10a8f06", "type": "concept", "title": "Partial pressures and diffusion"}, {"id": "7aff5f5c-bb6c-4ac5-9bac-607e3403b9b7", "type": "concept", "title": "Ventilation-perfusion matching"}]}, {"id": "a259f140-483b-4e74-b95e-cb5907f04ec7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Acid-base regulation", "description": "Learners connect breathing to pH and metabolic demands.", "children": [{"id": "730b1324-f527-4fea-be1f-9727e8e31bc5", "type": "concept", "title": "Carbon dioxide and bicarbonate buffer system"}, {"id": "2be930c9-a5d5-4117-8d6a-949980c34b50", "type": "concept", "title": "Respiratory acidosis and alkalosis basics"}, {"id": "27671270-418a-4026-81a9-9f9cb444be4c", "type": "concept", "title": "Exercise hyperventilation and pH regulation"}]}]}, {"id": "5b5476da-1131-4faa-a903-b86e241f6564", "type": "topic", "title": "Respiratory Physiology Lab: Spirometry, Ventilation, and Exercise Integration", "description": "Use lab methods to connect lung volumes, ventilation, and exercise intensity.", "children": [{"id": "b491a837-160a-4b4b-b471-defae98c2fcf", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Spirometry and lung volumes", "description": "Students use spirometry to measure lung function and understand respiratory capacity.", "children": [{"id": "7340b601-fd87-4e87-b545-a976c0658cfc", "type": "concept", "title": "Tidal volume, inspiratory reserve, expiratory reserve, vital capacity"}, {"id": "6a3b63e6-88e1-4e0b-bcc4-10f26b99d4a3", "type": "concept", "title": "FEV1, FVC, and FEV1/FVC concepts"}, {"id": "b86ac281-245e-43d5-a79a-800966f17c0f", "type": "concept", "title": "Predicted values and measurement technique"}]}, {"id": "094ce1ec-08b3-4d1b-8f28-cbee6f54e41f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Ventilation during exercise", "description": "The goal is to connect breathing patterns to metabolic demand.", "children": [{"id": "7791a101-3d7a-4471-bf04-6ada8b5e15b0", "type": "concept", "title": "Minute ventilation"}, {"id": "2cef0110-b242-43a1-a08b-19993591907e", "type": "concept", "title": "Respiratory rate and tidal volume changes"}, {"id": "0d4fa05f-0958-41c8-a040-37b2f78aebd0", "type": "concept", "title": "Ventilatory threshold overview"}]}, {"id": "24d65a49-6afb-498c-