icrobiome overview"}]}, {"id": "8582d8e4-d0fa-42cf-b048-65a0272bfd13", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Metabolism and energy balance", "description": "Learners connect nutrition to kinesiology and performance.", "children": [{"id": "1ed2a82e-09cb-4812-8de6-8b51e4ff2f13", "type": "concept", "title": "Basal metabolic rate and total daily energy expenditure"}, {"id": "29c1a836-942e-4ef5-825b-13580e64ec8c", "type": "concept", "title": "Glycogen, fat storage, and protein turnover"}, {"id": "03356bbb-9820-48d3-9d38-edafdbd330b5", "type": "concept", "title": "Fuel use at rest and during exercise"}]}]}, {"id": "0243f938-c306-47db-980e-a31e2019f5b3", "type": "topic", "title": "Urinary System, Renal Physiology, Fluid-Electrolyte Balance, and Hydration", "description": "Learn how the kidneys regulate volume, electrolytes, waste, pressure, and exercise-related hydration.", "children": [{"id": "9fba9e62-90b8-4f9f-8208-b62123b4ea92", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Renal anatomy", "description": "Students learn the structure of filtration and urine formation.", "children": [{"id": "844367de-d230-4032-ba11-92d72da54e67", "type": "concept", "title": "Kidneys, ureters, bladder, urethra"}, {"id": "0cd009b0-16ec-47ec-8182-452535708407", "type": "concept", "title": "Nephron anatomy"}, {"id": "5461ab82-a5a1-4548-89d4-765ef397bd1f", "type": "concept", "title": "Glomerulus, tubules, collecting ducts, and renal blood flow"}]}, {"id": "6d74cd09-d575-468d-8015-8ecb667e5ba6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Renal physiology", "description": "The point is to understand how kidneys regulate blood chemistry and volume.", "children": [{"id": "1ddf6753-1183-4787-bcca-71ca34aac843", "type": "concept", "title": "Filtration, reabsorption, secretion, and excretion"}, {"id": "2185f056-de00-4b37-9c08-c2a6d6d034e9", "type": "concept", "title": "GFR, clearance, and urine concentration"}, {"id": "22806ed8-1af2-4beb-8bf1-742fae2cd044", "type": "concept", "title": "Renin-angiotensin-aldosterone system and ADH"}]},